BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG-20260510-WA0158-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Walkthroughs,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20260827T123226Z
DESCRIPTION:Image Credits: Vidit Jain\nThis walk invites participants to move slowly\, attending closely to the many worlds that coexist within the same stretch of the city: ecological\, historical\, multispecies\, and everyday. Walking then becomes a way of sensing these plural worlds and the futures already being rehearsed within them.\n\nSimple prompts will guide attention along the way: What exists here that no map would show? Whose world is this\, and whose has it been? What futures are already present in this neighbourhood\, waiting to be noticed?\n\nThe walk begins at MAP and moves through Cubbon Park before concluding at the Central State Library. Along the route\, participants will sense and gather local\, place-based imaginations of the future\, considering urban ecologies\, recreation\, local economies\, and community.\n\nThe session will close with a collective reflection\, inviting participants to ask: What worlds did we walk through\, and which ones were invisible to us before today?\n\nThis event is part of Plural Worlds\, developed in collaboration with Lagori Collective and presented in conjunction with Beneath the Turning Sky.\n\n&nbsp\;
DTEND:20260905T063000Z
DTSTART:20260905T043000Z
SUMMARY:Futures Walk
